Release
=======

From the project root (`make help` lists targets):

    make pkg

writes **only** `librsvg-c-2.62.3.tar.xz` under `../pkg/`.
The tarball is source only;
packaging lives in git `dist/`, not in the public archive.
`rust/` is not included. `debug/` and test logs (`tests/*.log`,
`tests/*.trs`) are not part of the release tarball.
`make dist-release` is an alias of `pkg`.

    make crux

writes `../pkg/Pkgfile` next to that tarball. It does not run
`pkgmk` and does not install onto the host.

    make deb

builds Debian binary packages into `../debpkg/` via DESTDIR
(`debian/tmp`). It does not `dpkg -i` or `make install` onto
the live prefix.

    cd ../pkg
    gpg --detach-sign --armor librsvg-c-2.62.3.tar.xz
    sha256sum librsvg-c-2.62.3.tar.xz > SHA256SUMS
    gpg --detach-sign --armor SHA256SUMS
